### 1. Health check
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/health

### 2. Start crawler with query parameters (Depth 3, Max 50 pages)
POST http://localhost:8081/crawler/start?seedUrl=http://localhost:9000/page1.html&maxPages=20&maxDepth=3&allowedDomain=localhost

### 3. Start crawler with JSON body and custom job ID
POST http://localhost:8081/crawler/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "seedUrl": "http://localhost:9000/page1.html",
  "jobId": "lab-demo-job",
  "maxPages": 25,
  "maxDepth": 3,
  "allowedDomain": "localhost",
  "stayOnDomain": true,
  "requestTimeoutMs": 3000,
  "politenessDelayMs": 50
}

### 4. Check status of current / latest job
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/status

### 5. Check specific job details & live progress
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/jobs/lab-demo-job

### 6. Check specific job status only
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/jobs/lab-demo-job/status

### 7. List all registered crawl jobs
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/jobs

### 8. Get visited URLs (with pagination)
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/visited?jobId=lab-demo-job&page=0&size=10

### 9. Get discovered URLs (with pagination)
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/discovered?jobId=lab-demo-job&page=0&size=10

### 10. Inspect pending URLs in the frontier queue
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/queue?jobId=lab-demo-job

### 11. Inspect failed URLs and HTTP error reasons
GET http://localhost:8081/crawler/failed?jobId=lab-demo-job

### 12. Clear state for a specific job
DELETE http://localhost:8081/crawler/jobs/lab-demo-job/state

### 13. Clear legacy default crawler state
DELETE http://localhost:8081/crawler/state